<html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'>
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <title>SIH Presentation Guide</title>
    <style>
        body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; line-height: 1.6; margin: 40px; color: #333; }
        h1 { color: #2c3e50; border-bottom: 2px solid #3498db; padding-bottom: 10px; }
        h2 { color: #2980b9; margin-top: 30px; }
        h3 { color: #16a085; }
        p { font-size: 14px; margin-bottom: 15px; }
        ul { margin-bottom: 20px; }
        li { font-size: 14px; margin-bottom: 8px; }
        .highlight { background-color: #f1f8ff; border-left: 4px solid #3498db; padding: 15px; margin: 20px 0; font-style: italic; }
        .tech-box { border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 15px; border-radius: 5px; background-color: #fafafa; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <h1>SIH Project Presentation Script & Guide</h1>
    <p><em>Use this script to confidently present your project to the invigilator. It is written in simple, non-technical language so you can explain exactly how your platform works.</em></p>

    <div class="highlight">
        <strong>Pro Tip:</strong> Keep the dashboard open on your screen while speaking. Point to the screen when you mention a feature.
    </div>

    <h2>1. The Introduction (Start Here)</h2>
    <p><strong>You say:</strong> "Hello sir/ma'am. We are solving Problem Statement 26134. Today, there is a massive gap between what colleges teach and what companies actually need. Students are learning outdated topics, and companies are struggling to find job-ready candidates."</p>
    <p><strong>You say:</strong> "To solve this, we built a <strong>Data-Driven Curriculum Alignment Platform</strong>. It acts as a bridge between the Industry (Companies), the Academia (Colleges), and the Government (Admin). Let me show you how it works step-by-step."</p>

    <h2>2. Step-by-Step Walkthrough</h2>

    <h3>Step 1: The Company (Industry Demand)</h3>
    <p><em>(Action: Open the Company Dashboard on your screen)</em></p>
    <p><strong>You say:</strong> "First, we look at the Company Dashboard. Companies use our platform for three things:</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Post Jobs:</strong> They post their real hiring requirements. This gives our system live data on what skills are in demand.</li>
        <li><strong>Industry Consultation:</strong> Companies can officially report what emerging skills they will need in the next 6 to 12 months.</li>
        <li><strong>Validate Reports:</strong> They can look at the college's updated curriculum and click 'Validate' to confirm if the college is teaching the right things."</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Step 2: The Smart AI Brain (ML Engine)</h3>
    <p><strong>You say:</strong> "Now, how do we process this data? We built a smart AI engine in the background. It reads all the job postings and compares them with the College's syllabus. It doesn't just look for missing skills; it actually flags <strong>obsolete topics</strong> (like Turbo C++ or old versions of PHP) that colleges should remove."</p>

    <h3>Step 3: The College (Updating the Curriculum)</h3>
    <p><em>(Action: Switch to the College Dashboard)</em></p>
    <p><strong>You say:</strong> "Next is the College Dashboard. A college uploads their syllabus here. Our AI instantly generates a <strong>Gap Report</strong>."</p>
    <p><em>(Action: Point to a Gap Report on the screen)</em></p>
    <p><strong>You say:</strong> "As you can see, the report tells the college exactly which industry skills are missing and warns them about outdated topics. It even recommends specific courses to fill the gap. Once the college updates their curriculum, they click the <strong>'Mark Curriculum as Revised'</strong> button. This creates proof that the college actually took action."</p>

    <h3>Step 4: The Admin (The Big Picture)</h3>
    <p><em>(Action: Switch to the Admin Dashboard)</em></p>
    <p><strong>You say:</strong> "Finally, the Government or Admin needs to see the big picture to plan training programs. In the Admin Dashboard, they can see:"</p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Sector Growth:</strong> Which sector (like IT or Manufacturing) is growing fastest.</li>
        <li><strong>Proficiency Demand:</strong> Whether companies need Beginner, Intermediate, or Advanced level candidates.</li>
        <li><strong>Quality Indicators:</strong> Exactly how many colleges have revised their curriculum based on our data.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>You say:</strong> "This provides a continuous, evidence-based system to keep education aligned with industry needs."</p>

    <h2>3. Explaining Your Tech Stack (In Simple Terms)</h2>
    <p>If the invigilator asks: <em>"What technologies did you use to build this?"</em></p>
    
    <div class="tech-box">
        <p><strong>Frontend (The User Interface): React.js & Vite</strong><br>
        <em>Explain it as:</em> "We used React to build the screens you see. It makes the website very fast and smooth, just like a mobile app, without needing to reload the page."</p>

        <p><strong>Backend (The Traffic Controller): Node.js & Express</strong><br>
        <em>Explain it as:</em> "We used Node.js for our backend server. It safely handles user logins, connects the dashboards, and saves information securely."</p>

        <p><strong>Database (The Storage): SQLite & Prisma ORM</strong><br>
        <em>Explain it as:</em> "We used SQLite to store all our data—like user accounts, job postings, and reports. We used Prisma to talk to the database easily and securely."</p>

        <p><strong>AI & Analytics (The Smart Brain): Python & Flask</strong><br>
        <em>Explain it as:</em> "We created a separate Python engine. Python is the best language for data analysis. It runs our smart logic to compare text, find missing skills, and detect outdated topics."</p>
    </div>

    <h2>4. Final Closing Statement</h2>
    <p><strong>You say:</strong> "In conclusion, our platform doesn't just show data. It creates a complete loop: Companies signal demand -> AI analyzes the gap -> Colleges update their syllabus -> Admin tracks the progress. Thank you!"</p>

</body>
</html>
